241
00:10:11,219 --> 00:10:12,249
- Right. - Yes.

242
00:10:12,249 --> 00:10:13,349
No way.

243
00:10:13,349 --> 00:10:14,819
(She washes them separately.)

244
00:10:17,689 --> 00:10:19,219
- With an old toothbrush? - Yes.

245
00:10:19,759 --> 00:10:21,989
She stores all the old toothbrushes...

246
00:10:21,989 --> 00:10:23,329
- Of course. - and uses them.

247
00:10:24,659 --> 00:10:25,999
- Gosh, that's amazing. - She's so thorough.

248
00:10:25,999 --> 00:10:27,199
(Okay. I'm done with this too.)

249
00:10:27,899 --> 00:10:30,269
Nice.

250
00:10:33,399 --> 00:10:37,679
(She reassembles them right after cleaning them.)

251
00:10:37,679 --> 00:10:38,779
Great.

252
00:10:39,309 --> 00:10:40,549
I'm done.

253
00:10:45,949 --> 00:10:48,089
- You just run it with toothpaste. - Right.

254
00:10:48,089 --> 00:10:49,419
(Once she runs the washer with the used toothpaste tube,)

255
00:10:50,119 --> 00:10:52,389
(she's done cleaning the washer.)

256
00:10:53,689 --> 00:10:56,259
I have a separate box for recyclables.

257
00:10:56,759 --> 00:10:58,999
My place is small, so I don't have a place for recyclables.

258
00:10:58,999 --> 00:11:01,569
She's using the space very efficiently.

259
00:11:02,269 --> 00:11:03,269
(Oh, I almost forgot.)

260
00:11:05,439 --> 00:11:06,799
