261
00:11:09,539 --> 00:11:11,879
(This time, she puts on a mask.)

262
00:11:14,579 --> 00:11:17,579
(Ji Su grabs her phone...)

263
00:11:19,049 --> 00:11:23,249
(and goes into the bathroom.)

264
00:11:25,259 --> 00:11:26,519
- What? - My goodness.

265
00:11:29,029 --> 00:11:30,399
- It's my work song. - Yes.

266
00:11:30,529 --> 00:11:31,859
I put on baseball games.

267
00:11:32,129 --> 00:11:33,259
That's great.

268
00:11:37,969 --> 00:11:39,099
You clean the ceiling?

269
00:11:39,269 --> 00:11:40,439
- It's really dusty up there. - Nice.

270
00:11:40,869 --> 00:11:42,809
I've never seen anyone clean the ceiling.

271
00:11:43,609 --> 00:11:45,379
- It's really dusty up there. - Right.

272
00:11:45,379 --> 00:11:47,779
- It's the worst. - Cat fur goes up...

273
00:11:47,779 --> 00:11:49,279
- to the ceiling too. - Right.

274
00:11:49,279 --> 00:11:50,319
No way.

275
00:11:50,319 --> 00:11:52,449
(Diligently wiping the ceiling)

276
00:11:53,079 --> 00:11:54,449
I've been on this show for a decade.

277
00:11:54,449 --> 00:11:55,849
It's my first time seeing anyone clean the ceiling.

278
00:11:58,289 --> 00:11:59,389
That's crazy.

279
00:11:59,389 --> 00:12:00,589
(Wiping the entire ceiling)

280
00:12:03,059 --> 00:12:05,799
You can tell what someone is like...

281
00:12:05,799 --> 00:12:07,969
- just by looking at their bathroom. - Right!

282
00:12:07,969 --> 00:12:10,399
When you go over to someone's house, you can learn a lot...

283
00:12:10,539 --> 00:12:11,939
about their routine by looking at their bathroom.

284
00:12:11,939 --> 00:12:13,439
Like their daily routine.

285
00:12:13,599 --> 00:12:14,839
That's why I think...

286
00:12:14,839 --> 00:12:17,409
- bathrooms should always be clean. - I agree.

287
00:12:18,109 --> 00:12:21,949
So you're judging people by their bathroom?

288
00:12:22,079 --> 00:12:23,149
So it's...

289
00:12:23,149 --> 00:12:25,419
That's your inferiority complex talking.

290
00:12:26,149 --> 00:12:27,289
(Joking)

291
00:12:28,119 --> 00:12:30,359
(She puts down the mop she used to wipe the ceiling.)

292
00:12:31,289 --> 00:12:32,959
(Grabbing the next tool)

293
00:12:34,489 --> 00:12:35,689
- What's that? - What?

294
00:12:37,299 --> 00:12:38,699
- What's that? - What?

295
00:12:39,329 --> 00:12:40,699
- What's that? - What?

296
00:12:40,799 --> 00:12:42,299
- What? - I can't reach all the way up.

297
00:12:42,399 --> 00:12:44,799
That's a great product for short women like me.

298
00:12:44,799 --> 00:12:46,639
Once you spray it on the wall...

299
00:12:46,769 --> 00:12:48,509
- Does it get soaked? - It turns white.

300
00:12:48,509 --> 00:12:49,639
That's when you can wash it off.

301
00:12:49,639 --> 00:12:51,579
- It's like washing a car. - Yes.

302
00:12:52,009 --> 00:12:53,679
You can buy the same cleaning products I have.

303
00:12:53,809 --> 00:12:55,709
- I'm really going to buy them. - I see.

304
00:12:55,979 --> 00:12:58,719
- That's cost-efficient. - I only buy reasonably-priced ones.

305
00:12:59,579 --> 00:13:01,019
(Moved)

306
00:13:01,619 --> 00:13:03,819
(Spraying)

307
00:13:05,189 --> 00:13:06,319
My goodness.

308
00:13:06,319 --> 00:13:07,889
(Spraying over the entire wall)

309
00:13:09,729 --> 00:13:11,759
(There's no hesitation in her movement.)

310
00:13:13,329 --> 00:13:15,899
(Like an artist working on a masterpiece,)

311
00:13:17,599 --> 00:13:19,839
(her movements are bold and confident.)

312
00:13:19,839 --> 00:13:23,009
- My gosh. This is really necessary. - It is.

313
00:13:23,739 --> 00:13:24,739
(Spraying)

314
00:13:26,279 --> 00:13:27,279
(Spraying)

315
00:13:27,279 --> 00:13:28,579
Gosh, that's crazy.

316
00:13:31,619 --> 00:13:34,089
I use cleaning products...

317
00:13:34,089 --> 00:13:37,089
with skin-safe ingredients...

318
00:13:37,089 --> 00:13:40,019
to thoroughly clean the walls and the floor.

319
00:13:40,019 --> 00:13:41,889
(Showering the entire bathroom)

320
00:13:42,659 --> 00:13:44,529
(I'm done with the walls.)

321
00:13:45,059 --> 00:13:46,399
(A generous dollop of toothpaste)

322
00:13:46,399 --> 00:13:48,669
That's right. You should clean that.

323
00:13:50,199 --> 00:13:51,399
She cleans that too?

324
00:13:51,399 --> 00:13:53,269
- That's crazy. - This is great.

325
00:13:55,009 --> 00:13:56,409
(She quickly cleans the bottom of the sink.)

326
00:13:56,409 --> 00:13:58,479
- She works really fast. - This is crazy.

327
00:14:02,309 --> 00:14:03,849
(She scrubs the shower rail next.)

328
00:14:04,079 --> 00:14:05,879
My gosh. She's going above and beyond.

329
00:14:06,249 --> 00:14:07,489
There you go.

330
00:14:07,489 --> 00:14:09,019
Watching her clean is so satisfying.

331
00:14:10,419 --> 00:14:11,919
I really hate it...

332
00:14:11,919 --> 00:14:14,389
- when the shower rail gets rusty. - That's the worst.

333
00:14:14,389 --> 00:14:18,259
I use those toothbrushes with thin bristles to clean that.

334
00:14:18,259 --> 00:14:20,529
Just buy one and try cleaning it with the toothbrush.

335
00:14:21,929 --> 00:14:23,769
- That's it. - The gaps on the shower hose?

336
00:14:23,769 --> 00:14:25,999
- The hose is really dirty. - What?

337
00:14:26,399 --> 00:14:28,009
A lot of stains come off it.

338
00:14:28,009 --> 00:14:30,509
- So I clean the hose. - That's it.

339
00:14:32,709 --> 00:14:34,549
(Scrubbing hard with the toothbrush)

340
00:14:34,549 --> 00:14:36,709
Let me give you a tip.

341
00:14:36,909 --> 00:14:40,049
There's a brush with bristles on the back like toothbrushes.

342
00:14:40,049 --> 00:14:42,619
- You can use that and turn it. - That will be much better.

343
00:14:42,619 --> 00:14:43,649
That's much better for that.

344
00:14:43,649 --> 00:14:44,789
- Do you want a better tip? - I'm learning today.

345
00:14:44,789 --> 00:14:47,829
There's a shower hose without the gaps.

346
00:14:48,789 --> 00:14:51,499
(The cleaning seniors excitedly share cleaning tips.)

347
00:14:51,799 --> 00:14:53,499
There's a shower hose without the gaps.

348
00:14:53,499 --> 00:14:54,699
I'm learning so much today.

349
00:14:55,369 --> 00:14:57,769
- You should form a cleaning trio. - Right.

350
00:14:57,769 --> 00:14:59,339
- We should form a trio. - You guys can form one.

351
00:14:59,339 --> 00:15:01,039
- Sung Hwan too. - The three of you should do it.

352
00:15:01,039 --> 00:15:03,039
We can be the Cleanies.

353
00:15:03,039 --> 00:15:04,339
(They'd go by Cleanies.)

354
00:15:04,339 --> 00:15:05,409
- Great. - I love it.

355
00:15:05,409 --> 00:15:07,949
We should form a cleaning club.

356
00:15:09,449 --> 00:15:11,779
(The youngest Cleanie is almost done with the hose.)

357
00:15:14,449 --> 00:15:17,289
Looking at her eyes above the mask, I see a sense of incredible focus.

358
00:15:17,289 --> 00:15:18,489
- Right. I'm focused. - A sense of incredible focus.

359
00:15:19,119 --> 00:15:22,089
It's my dopamine rush. I love cleaning.

360
00:15:22,859 --> 00:15:26,129
When I was growing up, our bathroom was moldy.

361
00:15:26,299 --> 00:15:29,169
My mother always managed to get rid of the mold.

362
00:15:29,399 --> 00:15:32,169
When I saw that, I learned that I could get rid of mold...

363
00:15:32,169 --> 00:15:33,699
with some cleaning.

364
00:15:33,699 --> 00:15:35,469
- I learned that from my mom. - Yes, that's right.

365
00:15:36,139 --> 00:15:37,239
(She cleans...)

366
00:15:38,379 --> 00:15:40,009
(the inside of the toilet paper holder.)

367
00:15:40,009 --> 00:15:41,009
It's my dopamine rush.

368
00:15:41,349 --> 00:15:43,919
I never thought about cleaning the holder.

369
00:15:45,519 --> 00:15:47,589
- Gosh. She's so detailed. - That's where bugs come from.

370
00:15:47,589 --> 00:15:48,649
- I... - That's right.

371
00:15:49,119 --> 00:15:51,189
(Just like she learned from her mom...)

372
00:15:53,659 --> 00:15:54,689
Yes.

373
00:15:54,689 --> 00:15:55,689
(Clean and thorough)

374
00:15:55,689 --> 00:15:58,499
Then you have to remove the moisture.

375
00:15:59,459 --> 00:16:01,399
(Tiptoeing)

376
00:16:02,469 --> 00:16:06,439
(Splashing cold water on all of the walls)

377
00:16:08,309 --> 00:16:09,909
(Humming)

378
00:16:10,209 --> 00:16:12,579
Honestly, I bet it's cleaner than our body.

379
00:16:12,579 --> 00:16:13,779
- Right. - Yes.

380
00:16:15,149 --> 00:16:18,019
My gosh. I don't know what it is. But I'm getting hooked on this.

381
00:16:18,019 --> 00:16:19,119
I should look into that.

382
00:16:19,349 --> 00:16:21,249
How often do you deep-clean your bathroom like this?

383
00:16:21,249 --> 00:16:22,889
- I do it every week. - Yes. Right.

384
00:16:23,119 --> 00:16:24,359
I can totally relate to this.

385
00:16:24,359 --> 00:16:26,989
But I clean the toilet bowl whenever I take a shower...

386
00:16:27,089 --> 00:16:28,329
(I knew it.)

387
00:16:29,089 --> 00:16:30,289
(Another cleaner can relate.)

388
00:16:30,289 --> 00:16:32,329
- and every time I use the toilet. - That's...

389
00:16:32,959 --> 00:16:34,569
- My gosh. - That's something else.

390
00:16:34,869 --> 00:16:38,039
- Do you sometimes sleep in there? - Gosh, that's on another level.

391
00:16:38,539 --> 00:16:40,139
Why do you clean that thoroughly?

392
00:16:40,139 --> 00:16:42,309
I clean it to the point that I can sleep in there.

393
00:16:42,309 --> 00:16:43,369
- Right. - Yes.

394
00:16:44,939 --> 00:16:46,979
(This time, she grabs an orange towel.)

395
00:16:48,109 --> 00:16:50,449
(She steps on top of the toilet.)

396
00:16:51,649 --> 00:16:54,349
- We have the same cleaning towel. - It's good.

397
00:16:54,349 --> 00:16:55,419
- Really? - Yes.

398
00:16:56,819 --> 00:16:59,359
(Decalcomania)

399
00:17:01,759 --> 00:17:03,999
Do the towels have different purposes?

400
00:17:04,099 --> 00:17:05,899
- It's like... - I have face towels...

401
00:17:05,899 --> 00:17:07,059
- Yes. - and bath towels.

402
00:17:07,059 --> 00:17:08,069
- They're different towels? - They're different towels. Yes.

403
00:17:08,069 --> 00:17:10,129
For me, towels, rags, and dish towels are all the same.

404
00:17:10,939 --> 00:17:11,969
- Oh, no. - That's...

405
00:17:11,969 --> 00:17:13,269
- Oh, that's... - So all your towels are rags.

406
00:17:15,109 --> 00:17:17,479
(She's not done yet.)

407
00:17:18,179 --> 00:17:19,409
- Yes! - Removing moisture is...

408
00:17:19,409 --> 00:17:20,649
the most important part.

409
00:17:21,279 --> 00:17:22,909
I always do that after taking a shower.

410
00:17:24,379 --> 00:17:26,679
(Hopping)

411
00:17:29,049 --> 00:17:32,189
The most important last step of cleaning the bathroom is...

412
00:17:32,189 --> 00:17:33,389
removing moisture.

413
00:17:33,389 --> 00:17:37,259
I remove moisture after every time I take a shower.

414
00:17:37,259 --> 00:17:39,859
After cleaning the bathroom,

415
00:17:40,029 --> 00:17:42,769
always use the squeegee to remove moisture.

416
00:17:42,769 --> 00:17:45,169
Then your bathroom is twice as clean.

417
00:17:46,999 --> 00:17:50,139
Removing moisture is the most important for cleaning enthusiasts.

418
00:17:50,139 --> 00:17:52,179
Right. I don't know why, but watching her clean is satisfying.

419
00:17:54,449 --> 00:17:56,279
(She's finally done cleaning the bathroom.)

420
00:17:56,279 --> 00:17:57,519
It looks like a new house.

421
00:17:57,719 --> 00:17:59,079
Her landlord must be so happy.

422
00:18:00,019 --> 00:18:02,219
(Before and after the cleaning session)

423
00:18:02,219 --> 00:18:03,219
Great.

424
00:18:03,219 --> 00:18:04,719
- I don't see any difference. - Right?

425
00:18:04,719 --> 00:18:06,819
- I don't see any difference either. - It looks the same.

426
00:18:07,389 --> 00:18:08,689
- It's so clean. - It is.

427
00:18:08,689 --> 00:18:09,889
- Just like that... - It's super clean.

428
00:18:10,659 --> 00:18:12,359
- The fact that it looks the same... - Well, it's...

429
00:18:12,359 --> 00:18:13,759
- is cooler. - Right.

430
00:18:13,759 --> 00:18:15,669
- It's always clean. - Is it like being on a diet...

431
00:18:15,669 --> 00:18:17,699
- all the time? - That's right.

432
00:18:17,699 --> 00:18:18,999
- And the tiles... - No.

433
00:18:18,999 --> 00:18:20,769
- That was meant for me, right? - No.

434
00:18:20,769 --> 00:18:21,869
Let me clarify something.

435
00:18:22,439 --> 00:18:24,009
That's your inferiority complex creeping in.

436
00:18:24,009 --> 00:18:25,079
It is?

437
00:18:25,479 --> 00:18:27,039
- I was trying to understand it... - Okay.

438
00:18:27,039 --> 00:18:28,609
- from my point of view. - Okay.

439
00:18:28,609 --> 00:18:30,209
I have an inferiority complex.

440
00:18:30,209 --> 00:18:32,019
- I do too. - I do.

441
00:18:32,019 --> 00:18:33,279
- It's easier when you admit it. - Of course.

442
00:18:33,279 --> 00:18:35,149
- Everyone has it. - We all have it.

443
00:18:36,389 --> 00:18:37,489
Great.

444
00:18:37,659 --> 00:18:38,819
You have to turn on the fan...

445
00:18:38,819 --> 00:18:40,519
- and close the door. - Right.

446
00:18:40,729 --> 00:18:42,189
- You can't keep the door open. - Right.

447
00:18:42,329 --> 00:18:43,589
- I see. Really? - I see.

448
00:18:46,059 --> 00:18:49,169
(Gosh, I'm finally done.)

449
00:18:50,269 --> 00:18:52,839
(She wraps it up perfectly.)

450
00:18:53,899 --> 00:18:56,639
(Let me see.)

451
00:18:57,979 --> 00:19:00,139
- What's that? - I checked off what I did.

452
00:19:00,309 --> 00:19:01,379
That's nice.

453
00:19:01,379 --> 00:19:03,009
(Marking the cleaning task done on the planner)

454
00:19:03,749 --> 00:19:06,649
(Okay. I did it.)

455
00:19:07,949 --> 00:19:10,519
(After she finishes cleaning,)

456
00:19:10,519 --> 00:19:13,389
(she grabs her phone.)

457
00:19:19,159 --> 00:19:20,259
Why don't you lie down?

458
00:19:20,299 --> 00:19:22,129
I don't lie down again once I make the bed.

459
00:19:22,129 --> 00:19:23,199
- Right. - I see.

460
00:19:23,429 --> 00:19:24,799
- Not to lie down, - Yes.

461
00:19:24,799 --> 00:19:26,199
- you sat there instead. - Yes.

462
00:19:26,199 --> 00:19:28,409
(She's resting in front of the bathroom.)

463
00:19:29,209 --> 00:19:32,979
(She quietly checks her phone.)

464
00:19:34,149 --> 00:19:35,349
(Opening her banking app)

465
00:19:35,349 --> 00:19:36,449
A banking app?

466
00:19:38,119 --> 00:19:41,149
(Tapping)

467
00:19:42,649 --> 00:19:44,489
What? You wired some money.

468
00:19:44,489 --> 00:19:45,589
- Yes. - What?

469
00:19:45,589 --> 00:19:46,589
What's going on?

470
00:19:47,359 --> 00:19:50,659
I had a student loan.

471
00:19:50,659 --> 00:19:53,599
But I paid off all of my student loans as of today.

472
00:19:53,659 --> 00:19:55,229
- What? Really? - My gosh.

473
00:19:56,299 --> 00:19:57,769
(Congratulations!)

474
00:19:57,769 --> 00:19:59,269
Congratulations.

475
00:19:59,469 --> 00:20:02,039
- I got paid from my part-time job. - Okay.

476
00:20:02,269 --> 00:20:04,179
- What part-time job? - A part-time job?

477
00:20:04,179 --> 00:20:05,209
- Pardon? - What part-time job?

478
00:20:05,209 --> 00:20:06,909
I work part-time at a restaurant...

479
00:20:06,909 --> 00:20:09,449
and as a babysitter.

480
00:20:09,849 --> 00:20:11,419
Do you still work part-time?

481
00:20:11,419 --> 00:20:12,519
Yes, I do.

482
00:20:12,749 --> 00:20:14,589
Don't people recognize you?

483
00:20:14,589 --> 00:20:16,419
A lot of people recognize me.

484
00:20:16,619 --> 00:20:19,419
I had people come back after an hour when they saw me work...

485
00:20:19,419 --> 00:20:20,519
just to give me vitamin supplements.

486
00:20:21,659 --> 00:20:22,789
I really hope things work out for you.

487
00:20:22,789 --> 00:20:25,099
- I agree. I want to root for you. - Yes. I'm sure you will.

488
00:20:26,029 --> 00:20:27,599
It's been nine years.

489
00:20:28,029 --> 00:20:30,599
It took a long time because I had to pay it back with my part-time jobs.

490
00:20:31,899 --> 00:20:35,239
"Come and check this out." I once gave out flyers...

491
00:20:35,239 --> 00:20:36,969
while wearing a cat costume.

492
00:20:37,109 --> 00:20:41,409
I paid it back with my hard-earned money from my part-time jobs.

493
00:20:42,249 --> 00:20:43,279
- Gosh. - That's amazing.

494
00:20:43,279 --> 00:20:44,979
- Your parents didn't help you? - Seriously.

495
00:20:45,179 --> 00:20:47,489
They asked me if I wanted their help.

496
00:20:47,489 --> 00:20:48,919
But it was my education.

497
00:20:48,919 --> 00:20:50,859
- My mom didn't attend the school. - Right.

498
00:20:50,859 --> 00:20:53,459
- My gosh. - It's only right I paid it back.

499
00:20:53,959 --> 00:20:55,189
My gosh, no.

500
00:20:55,559 --> 00:20:57,289
- Usually, kids accept help. - I love her mindset.

501
00:20:57,289 --> 00:20:59,299
They promise to pay it back twofold.

502
00:20:59,299 --> 00:21:00,799
- You know? - That's usually the case.

503
00:21:00,799 --> 00:21:02,669
It was my education, and my mom paid for it,

504
00:21:02,669 --> 00:21:03,929
but I still skipped classes.

505
00:21:03,929 --> 00:21:05,999
- And people don't pay it back. - Hey.

506
00:21:05,999 --> 00:21:07,939
I did all of that. And I told my mom...

507
00:21:07,939 --> 00:21:09,209
I was taking time off from school...

508
00:21:09,209 --> 00:21:10,509
and asked her to give me the tuition.

509
00:21:12,179 --> 00:21:13,939
- Ji Su, you're so cool. - That's really cool.

510
00:21:13,939 --> 00:21:15,309
- Seriously. - Gosh, Ji Su.

511
00:21:15,309 --> 00:21:17,649
It was my education. So...

512
00:21:17,649 --> 00:21:20,719
- You're emotional. Great job. - My gosh. You did well.

513
00:21:20,719 --> 00:21:21,789
- Gosh. - Goodness.

514
00:21:22,019 --> 00:21:23,619
- What? - Give her some pocket money.

515
00:21:24,789 --> 00:21:26,159
(Blinking)

516
00:21:26,389 --> 00:21:28,329
- What am I? Her grandpa? - Come on.

517
00:21:28,329 --> 00:21:30,529
- Why would I give her money? - Come on, give her some money.

518
00:21:30,529 --> 00:21:32,699
- You can give her some money. - I don't have cash on me.

519
00:21:32,699 --> 00:21:34,099
- I'll give it to you later. - Okay.

520
00:21:34,929 --> 00:21:36,969
(Grandpa is the best.)

521
00:21:37,569 --> 00:21:38,899
(She paid back the student loan in 9 years.)

522
00:21:38,899 --> 00:21:40,399
- I'm reevaluating myself now. - She did that...

523
00:21:40,399 --> 00:21:41,869
- while building her career. - I couldn't have done that.

524
00:21:43,209 --> 00:21:46,639
(Thinking)

525
00:21:47,379 --> 00:21:48,509
(She calls someone.)

526
00:21:48,509 --> 00:21:50,449
What is it? Who are you calling?

527
00:21:50,449 --> 00:21:51,819
(She calls someone.)

528
00:21:53,419 --> 00:21:54,949
- Hello. - Mom, what are you doing?

529
00:21:55,619 --> 00:21:57,119
- Hello. - Mom, what are you doing?

530
00:21:57,959 --> 00:21:59,119
- Me? - Yes.

531
00:21:59,319 --> 00:22:00,659
I'm home.

532
00:22:01,029 --> 00:22:03,029
I just...

533
00:22:03,659 --> 00:22:07,999
made the last payment of my student loan.

534
00:22:08,469 --> 00:22:09,469
My goodness.

535
00:22:10,399 --> 00:22:12,139
Great job, Ji Su.

536
00:22:14,339 --> 00:22:16,239
Gosh, that must have been tough.

537
00:22:18,739 --> 00:22:19,739
Ji Su.

538
00:22:20,709 --> 00:22:22,209
You worked so hard to pay it off.

539
00:22:23,549 --> 00:22:24,649
I'm sorry...

540
00:22:25,579 --> 00:22:27,349
I couldn't help you more.

541
00:22:27,379 --> 00:22:29,789
- Gosh, she's emotional too. - My gosh.

542
00:22:31,019 --> 00:22:32,819
- My gosh. - I'm so proud of you, Ji Su.

543
00:22:34,059 --> 00:22:36,759
No, you already helped me plenty.

544
00:22:36,889 --> 00:22:40,529
(Choking up)

545
00:22:41,229 --> 00:22:43,099
My goodness.

546
00:22:43,099 --> 00:22:44,299
(You worked so hard.)

547
00:22:44,299 --> 00:22:46,039
- Gosh. You must've worked hard. - Oh, my.

548
00:22:46,099 --> 00:22:47,969
Oh, no. I cry easily.

549
00:22:47,969 --> 00:22:50,009
(Sobbing)

550
00:22:50,069 --> 00:22:52,179
- She paid it back in nine years. - I also cry easily.

551
00:22:52,179 --> 00:22:54,549
- It's okay. - It must've bothered her mom.

552
00:22:56,479 --> 00:22:58,119
The memories from that day are coming back.

553
00:22:58,119 --> 00:22:59,549
- I see. - It's okay.

554
00:23:00,149 --> 00:23:01,149
Hyun Moo will give you...

555
00:23:01,149 --> 00:23:02,149
- pocket money. - That's right.

556
00:23:02,149 --> 00:23:03,149
- How much should I give her? - He'll do everything.

557
00:23:03,149 --> 00:23:04,189
He'll buy you a house too.

558
00:23:04,189 --> 00:23:05,759
(Quickly trying to help her stop crying)

559
00:23:06,219 --> 00:23:08,889
I'm debt-free now.

560
00:23:09,659 --> 00:23:11,099
Yes, you're debt-free.

561
00:23:11,099 --> 00:23:14,029
Ji Su, only good things will be in your future.

562
00:23:14,699 --> 00:23:16,999
- Okay. - I'll root for you.

563
00:23:17,769 --> 00:23:18,869
Thank you.

564
00:23:19,669 --> 00:23:21,739
Don't thank me. I should thank you.

565
00:23:22,409 --> 00:23:23,439
I'm sorry too.

566
00:23:24,239 --> 00:23:28,349
Today, I'm going to buy some things I wanted to buy.

567
00:23:28,349 --> 00:23:29,409
My gosh.

568
00:23:29,449 --> 00:23:32,219
Buy whatever you want and eat whatever you crave too.

569
00:23:32,349 --> 00:23:34,749
And do everything you couldn't do before. Okay?

570
00:23:34,889 --> 00:23:35,889
Okay.

571
00:23:36,789 --> 00:23:40,159
I'll buy you a lot of things later too.

572
00:23:40,859 --> 00:23:42,829
Okay. Buy me a lot of things later.

573
00:23:43,859 --> 00:23:44,899
Okay.

574
00:23:46,599 --> 00:23:48,369
Thank you for everything, Mom.

575
00:23:48,629 --> 00:23:51,839
This is a happy day for both of us. Right?

576
00:23:51,839 --> 00:23:52,869
That's right.

577
00:23:53,139 --> 00:23:54,939
Yes. Have a good day today.

578
00:23:55,039 --> 00:23:57,339
Okay. I love you, Mom.

579
00:23:57,409 --> 00:23:59,579
- Okay. Have a good day. - Okay.

580
00:23:59,579 --> 00:24:01,679
- You too. - Thanks.

581
00:24:01,679 --> 00:24:06,049
(She finishes the call with a warm goodbye.)

582
00:24:24,229 --> 00:24:26,769
- My goodness. - Gosh, an experience like that...

583
00:24:26,999 --> 00:24:28,839
- This is quite emotional indeed. - Right.

584
00:24:30,869 --> 00:24:32,679
It was odd. I felt empty inside.

585
00:24:33,709 --> 00:24:35,449
Actually, I didn't think I'd cry.

586
00:24:36,209 --> 00:24:39,279
I know I cry easily. But I thought I would be full of smiles today.

587
00:24:39,519 --> 00:24:42,089
"This is crazy. It's over!" I thought I'd celebrate like this.

588
00:24:42,719 --> 00:24:44,519
"I did this."

589
00:24:44,759 --> 00:24:46,419
"I was someone who could do this."

590
00:24:46,619 --> 00:24:48,589
That was the first thought I had.

591
00:24:48,589 --> 00:24:50,529
Then I felt empty...

592
00:24:50,529 --> 00:24:52,629
- and thought of my mom. - Feeling empty is understandable.

593
00:24:53,429 --> 00:24:54,829
You feel empty...

594
00:24:54,829 --> 00:24:56,069
because you've worked hard.

595
00:24:56,229 --> 00:24:57,869
When I hung up,

596
00:24:58,269 --> 00:24:59,999
- the past nine years... - That's right.

597
00:24:59,999 --> 00:25:01,039
flitted through my mind.

598
00:25:01,039 --> 00:25:03,339
The part-time jobs flitted through my mind.

599
00:25:03,969 --> 00:25:05,939
- Your parents must be proud. - Seriously.

600
00:25:05,939 --> 00:25:08,049
- Seriously. - They must be very proud.

601
00:25:13,579 --> 00:25:16,619
(Rushing over)

602
00:25:17,449 --> 00:25:18,489
Gamja.

603
00:25:19,589 --> 00:25:21,259
A cat consoles her.

604
00:25:21,629 --> 00:25:23,029
- Gamja. - How did she come to her right now?

605
00:25:23,829 --> 00:25:25,659
She comes to me whenever I cry.

606
00:25:27,499 --> 00:25:29,799
(After consoling her mom,)

607
00:25:29,799 --> 00:25:32,099
(she goes back to her place in a chic way.)

608
00:25:33,439 --> 00:25:37,139
(Thanks to Gamja, she pulls herself together.)

609
00:25:39,379 --> 00:25:41,209
(Heave-ho)

610
00:25:43,709 --> 00:25:45,349
(She changes to go out.)

611
00:25:45,349 --> 00:25:46,549
I guess she'll buy something.

612
00:25:50,719 --> 00:25:52,559
(She packs her bag.)

613
00:25:53,719 --> 00:25:56,959
(Let's go shopping.)

614
00:25:58,729 --> 00:26:01,229
(Humming)

615
00:26:02,129 --> 00:26:03,199
It's nice.

616
00:26:03,869 --> 00:26:05,069
The weather is so nice.

617
00:26:06,769 --> 00:26:09,269
There is something I want to do...

618
00:26:09,269 --> 00:26:10,509
when I pay off my student loans.

619
00:26:10,769 --> 00:26:13,179
It's buying unexpected items.

620
00:26:13,909 --> 00:26:17,679
I want to buy the items I want without any worries.

621
00:26:20,019 --> 00:26:23,189
(I'll buy everything I want today.)

622
00:26:23,189 --> 00:26:24,759
I'm curious to see how Ji Su will flex.

623
00:26:25,059 --> 00:26:26,419
Had it been like that

624
00:26:26,419 --> 00:26:27,719
Maybe she'll only buy the cleaning supplies.

625
00:26:28,259 --> 00:26:30,189
(Laughing)

626
00:26:31,499 --> 00:26:35,069
I'm really curious to see what Ji Su will buy.

627
00:26:36,199 --> 00:26:38,439
Let's clear the place.

628
00:26:42,969 --> 00:26:44,509
See? She went to Daiso.

629
00:26:46,179 --> 00:26:47,879
(Her eyes become lively.)

630
00:26:49,209 --> 00:26:51,619
(What should I buy?)

631
00:26:52,449 --> 00:26:55,119
(Her feet lead her to a place.)

632
00:26:56,549 --> 00:26:58,319
(A cleaning supplies section?)

633
00:26:58,319 --> 00:27:00,059
See? It's cleaning again.

634
00:27:00,219 --> 00:27:01,829
I wasn't going to go there.

635
00:27:01,959 --> 00:27:03,289
It's her idea of flexing.

636
00:27:04,059 --> 00:27:05,059
All right.

637
00:27:05,059 --> 00:27:06,699
(Let's see.)

638
00:27:06,699 --> 00:27:07,699
All right.

639
00:27:08,669 --> 00:27:09,699
(Sparkling eyes)

640
00:27:09,699 --> 00:27:10,699
(Which product is better?)

641
00:27:10,699 --> 00:27:11,769
Which one is better?

642
00:27:14,369 --> 00:27:15,769
(I choose you.)

643
00:27:15,769 --> 00:27:17,939
I'll remember the items Ji Su buys.

644
00:27:18,279 --> 00:27:19,409
I'll buy them as well.

645
00:27:19,409 --> 00:27:20,409
(This one...)

646
00:27:20,809 --> 00:27:21,909
(and that one)

647
00:27:25,879 --> 00:27:27,379
She is flexing.

648
00:27:27,819 --> 00:27:30,749
She paid off her debts. It's a good day to flex.

649
00:27:30,749 --> 00:27:31,959
I agree.

650
00:27:34,189 --> 00:27:37,359
(Very satisfied)

651
00:27:39,399 --> 00:27:41,869
(She takes out the grocery bag she has brought from home.)

652
00:27:42,899 --> 00:27:44,429
(Flexing properly)

653
00:27:44,429 --> 00:27:45,939
Will the total be about 50 dollars?

654
00:27:47,744 --> 00:27:49,084
(18 items cost 35.5 dollars.)

655
00:27:49,109 --> 00:27:50,409
I flexed.

656
00:27:51,479 --> 00:27:54,209
I usually spend only ten dollars when I go to Daiso.

657
00:27:54,209 --> 00:27:56,249
I usually spend only 10 dollars. Today, I spent 30 dollars.

658
00:27:56,249 --> 00:27:59,719
I spent three times the money.

659
00:28:02,449 --> 00:28:03,819
Thank you.

660
00:28:05,259 --> 00:28:06,459
(I enjoyed overspending.)

661
00:28:06,459 --> 00:28:07,459
Gamja.

662
00:28:10,559 --> 00:28:12,159
Did she come home right away?

663
00:28:12,159 --> 00:28:13,459
- Yes. - That's right.

664
00:28:13,629 --> 00:28:14,769
Why didn't she eat anything?

665
00:28:14,769 --> 00:28:16,429
- Mom told her to eat tasty food. - She came home really quickly.

666
00:28:16,429 --> 00:28:18,939
- I wasn't used to spending money, - That's right.

667
00:28:18,939 --> 00:28:20,469
so I didn't know where to go.

668
00:28:20,469 --> 00:28:22,769
You should've eaten tasty food at a nice restaurant...

669
00:28:22,769 --> 00:28:24,709
- That's right. - and bought clothes.

670
00:28:24,709 --> 00:28:26,109
I rarely buy clothes.

671
00:28:26,109 --> 00:28:27,109
- Really? - Yes.

672
00:28:27,109 --> 00:28:29,609
I maybe buy one piece of clothing a month.

673
00:28:29,909 --> 00:28:32,019
I'm not telling you to splurge.

674
00:28:32,419 --> 00:28:34,319
But if there were items you liked, you should buy them...

675
00:28:34,319 --> 00:28:36,289
- or try them on. - Think of your interests.

676
00:28:36,289 --> 00:28:37,449
But you suppress your urges.

677
00:28:37,449 --> 00:28:38,919
She has gotten used to it.

678
00:28:38,919 --> 00:28:40,219
- That's right. - Yes.

679
00:28:40,589 --> 00:28:41,729
- I don't have many clothes, - Nothing like that.

680
00:28:41,729 --> 00:28:43,159
but I want to buy her clothes.

681
00:28:43,159 --> 00:28:44,729
You should buy your own clothes.

682
00:28:46,129 --> 00:28:48,529
- I just want to buy her clothes. - Seriously.

683
00:28:50,599 --> 00:28:53,039
(Picking up)

684
00:28:55,039 --> 00:28:56,269
(She sanitizes her phone upon coming home.)

685
00:28:56,269 --> 00:28:58,109
- I can't believe it. - She is neat.

686
00:29:06,019 --> 00:29:08,589
(She changes into comfortable clothes.)

687
00:29:09,749 --> 00:29:11,919
(Rattling)

688
00:29:14,959 --> 00:29:19,599
(It's time to eat dinner.)

689
00:29:23,499 --> 00:29:24,839
(She takes out a scale.)

690
00:29:24,839 --> 00:29:28,009
Will she measure the grams? She uses a scale.

691
00:29:32,209 --> 00:29:34,709
(She pours in cream without hesitation.)

692
00:29:35,279 --> 00:29:37,649
(She pours in the exact amount of sugar.)

693
00:29:37,649 --> 00:29:41,149
Today, I want to bake something.

694
00:29:41,149 --> 00:29:43,889
I'll make a strawberry cream cake.

695
00:29:44,019 --> 00:29:45,519
- A strawberry cream cake? - A strawberry cream cake?

696
00:29:45,519 --> 00:29:47,219
(That's incredible.)

697
00:29:49,359 --> 00:29:50,389
What?

698
00:29:52,729 --> 00:29:56,369
(Another appliance, an electric mixer, appears.)

699
00:29:56,369 --> 00:29:58,639
She has skills from working part-time.

700
00:29:58,639 --> 00:30:00,069
She knows how to use those appliances.

701
00:30:01,709 --> 00:30:04,009
(Thanks to the appliance, the cream is whipped in no time.)

702
00:30:04,139 --> 00:30:05,209
All right.

703
00:30:05,539 --> 00:30:07,779
(Taking out)

704
00:30:09,249 --> 00:30:10,549
(Moon-shaped bread)

705
00:30:10,549 --> 00:30:11,849
You know what it is.

706
00:30:12,779 --> 00:30:13,779
It's a nice tip.

707
00:30:13,779 --> 00:30:14,819
- It's a nice tip. - That's right.

708
00:30:14,819 --> 00:30:16,789
You use it as a sheet cake.

709
00:30:16,949 --> 00:30:18,719
- Full Moon Cake. - I prepared it on purpose.

710
00:30:20,519 --> 00:30:23,229
(She brushes on sugar water on the halved cake.)

711
00:30:25,599 --> 00:30:26,729
She has everything.

712
00:30:27,159 --> 00:30:29,269
I sometimes buy those kinds of things.

713
00:30:30,969 --> 00:30:34,839
(She puts a heap of whipped cream on the top.)

714
00:30:35,669 --> 00:30:38,039
(She puts fresh strawberries between the sheets.)

715
00:30:39,439 --> 00:30:41,549
(She turns the turntable to spread the whipped cream.)

716
00:30:41,549 --> 00:30:42,679
The cake is coming along.

717
00:30:46,179 --> 00:30:47,349
- That's right. - It looks pretty.

718
00:30:47,819 --> 00:30:49,389
It looks like an actual cake.

719
00:30:50,689 --> 00:30:52,789
(Squeezing)

720
00:30:52,789 --> 00:30:55,159
(Piping)

721
00:30:57,629 --> 00:30:58,759
- Well done. - It's pretty.

722
00:30:58,759 --> 00:31:00,029
(She wraps up with strawberry decorations.)

723
00:31:01,729 --> 00:31:02,799
Good.

724
00:31:03,199 --> 00:31:05,839
- Did you make that at home? - Yes.

725
00:31:06,139 --> 00:31:08,039
- I'm impressed. - Anyone can make it.

726
00:31:08,939 --> 00:31:10,609
(She puts the cake in the fridge...)

727
00:31:10,609 --> 00:31:12,809
(and plops down.)

728
00:31:13,279 --> 00:31:14,279
(I'm exhausted.)

729
00:31:14,279 --> 00:31:18,049
(To be continued)

730
00:31:18,349 --> 00:31:19,419
Is someone here?

731
00:31:19,619 --> 00:31:20,819
Teacher? Mom?

732
00:31:22,236 --> 00:31:25,836
(Ji Su runs over to get the door upon hearing the bell.)

733
00:31:25,836 --> 00:31:26,976
Ji Su, hello.

734
00:31:27,806 --> 00:31:29,276
(Stomping)

735
00:31:30,146 --> 00:31:31,246
- Who is that? - Who is that?

736
00:31:31,706 --> 00:31:32,746
My goodness.

737
00:31:32,746 --> 00:31:34,376
- Dad, come on in. - Hello.

738
00:31:34,476 --> 00:31:36,086
- Who is that? - My dad.

739
00:31:37,846 --> 00:31:39,086
- Water. - Do you welcome your dad...

740
00:31:39,086 --> 00:31:40,356
that warmly?

741
00:31:40,886 --> 00:31:42,926
Your dad must love you so much.

742
00:31:44,386 --> 00:31:47,896
There was a reason to celebrate,

743
00:31:47,896 --> 00:31:49,226
so I invited Dad to my place.

744
00:31:50,266 --> 00:31:51,366
Dad, thanks for the water.

745
00:31:51,366 --> 00:31:54,236
- I only had one bottle left. - Really?

746
00:31:54,236 --> 00:31:56,966
Dad always brings it because it's heavy.

747
00:31:56,966 --> 00:31:58,136
(Oh, my)

748
00:31:58,136 --> 00:31:59,436
- Right now, - So...

749
00:31:59,636 --> 00:32:01,736
- it needs to be wiped down. - I'll do it.

750
00:32:02,076 --> 00:32:04,006
- I need to taste it. - Chicken soup?

751
00:32:04,006 --> 00:32:05,516
- Did you make chicken soup? - I know.

752
00:32:05,516 --> 00:32:06,916
- No way. - When did you make that?

753
00:32:06,916 --> 00:32:08,076
(She made tasty chicken soup earlier.)

754
00:32:08,076 --> 00:32:10,286
- She boiled chicken. - She is diligent.

755
00:32:10,286 --> 00:32:11,386
(Full of love)

756
00:32:11,786 --> 00:32:13,656
- My goodness. - I made chicken soup.

757
00:32:13,656 --> 00:32:14,886
- He must be so happy. - It's nearly done.

758
00:32:14,986 --> 00:32:17,056
Where is Gamja?

759
00:32:17,056 --> 00:32:18,626
- Under the table. - Where is Gamja?

760
00:32:19,496 --> 00:32:21,496
- Gamja won't come out. - Let's see.

761
00:32:21,626 --> 00:32:22,896
Gamja, it's good to see you.

762
00:32:23,696 --> 00:32:24,726
It's good to see you.

763
00:32:25,296 --> 00:32:27,966
- Dad, did you look behind you? - What?

764
00:32:28,236 --> 00:32:29,366
- Say hello. - What?

765
00:32:29,536 --> 00:32:31,506
- Hello. - Hello.

766
00:32:31,706 --> 00:32:33,836
In 1, 2... In 1, 2, 3.

767
00:32:33,976 --> 00:32:34,976
- Hello. - Hello.

768
00:32:34,976 --> 00:32:37,006
- I've seen him many times on TV. - We've seen you many times on TV.

769
00:32:37,006 --> 00:32:39,176
- He is my dad. - Nice to meet you.

770
00:32:39,176 --> 00:32:40,816
Hello. Let's do it one last time.

771
00:32:41,176 --> 00:32:42,246
Hello.

772
00:32:42,786 --> 00:32:45,046
It's so nice that you guys are like friends.

773
00:32:45,286 --> 00:32:47,116
- I'll sit here. - It won't take long.

774
00:32:47,116 --> 00:32:49,526
(Dad, please wait a second.)

775
00:32:50,456 --> 00:32:52,096
Dad, yours is coming first.

776
00:32:52,096 --> 00:32:53,526
Be careful.

777
00:32:53,526 --> 00:32:54,956
(She scoops her dad's chicken soup first.)

778
00:32:56,796 --> 00:32:58,366
- Is there yours as well? - Of course.

779
00:32:58,936 --> 00:33:00,696
- Dad, this is mine. - Okay.

780
00:33:00,696 --> 00:33:02,466
I hope you'll give me some meat.

781
00:33:02,732 --> 00:33:03,732
What?

782
00:33:04,632 --> 00:33:06,902
- I hope you'll give me some meat. - Okay.

783
00:33:09,602 --> 00:33:11,242
My pot is small.

784
00:33:11,242 --> 00:33:13,042
It didn't fit two chickens.

785
00:33:13,042 --> 00:33:14,542
- I could only cook one chicken. - Hold on.

786
00:33:14,542 --> 00:33:15,912
There is no meat whatsoever.

787
00:33:16,482 --> 00:33:17,512
Give me your plate.

788
00:33:17,512 --> 00:33:19,412
That's more than enough.

789
00:33:19,412 --> 00:33:20,712
- Take one. - Okay.

790
00:33:23,452 --> 00:33:25,022
- It looks legit. - Does it look legit?

791
00:33:25,022 --> 00:33:26,592
Let's try it.

792
00:33:27,122 --> 00:33:28,862
- The soup. - All right.

793
00:33:28,862 --> 00:33:30,362
(She tries the soup first.)

794
00:33:30,362 --> 00:33:32,462
The soup.

795
00:33:32,462 --> 00:33:35,162
(Dad takes a bite.)

796
00:33:35,162 --> 00:33:36,162
(I see.)

797
00:33:38,232 --> 00:33:40,302
- Was it your first time making it? - Yes, it was my first time.

798
00:33:40,302 --> 00:33:42,072
- Really? - It was my first time.

799
00:33:43,772 --> 00:33:44,802
(Thumbs up)

800
00:33:44,802 --> 00:33:46,342
- What? He gave a thumbs-up. - Is it tasty? Is it good?

801
00:33:46,572 --> 00:33:47,912
You need to add salt.

802
00:33:48,542 --> 00:33:50,982
Firstly, you've worked hard.

803
00:33:51,612 --> 00:33:52,712
You've worked hard.

804
00:33:53,082 --> 00:33:54,582
(Relieved)

805
00:33:55,782 --> 00:33:57,352
Dad, you're eating with gusto.

806
00:33:57,352 --> 00:33:58,822
He is enjoying his food.

807
00:33:59,152 --> 00:34:00,422
He is eating with gusto.

808
00:34:00,422 --> 00:34:01,792
- Dad eats with gusto. - Yes.

809
00:34:01,792 --> 00:34:02,792
(Taking another bite)

810
00:34:03,162 --> 00:34:04,662
- Today, - I heard it.

811
00:34:04,822 --> 00:34:07,632
I paid off my student loans.

812
00:34:07,632 --> 00:34:08,832
- That's right. - Yes.

813
00:34:09,462 --> 00:34:10,862
Well done. Let's go.

814
00:34:11,932 --> 00:34:13,932
Let's go. You've done so well.

815
00:34:14,872 --> 00:34:17,002
(Proud)

816
00:34:17,102 --> 00:34:19,412
You were a nominee at the Baeksang Arts Awards.

817
00:34:20,742 --> 00:34:22,172
I felt very proud.

818
00:34:22,172 --> 00:34:23,412
Of course, he felt proud.

819
00:34:24,212 --> 00:34:27,212
- Winning an award wasn't important. - That's right.

820
00:34:27,212 --> 00:34:29,552
I felt like I was dreaming.

821
00:34:30,022 --> 00:34:31,452
You just need to enjoy yourself.

822
00:34:31,452 --> 00:34:32,592
That's right.

823
00:34:33,292 --> 00:34:35,292
I think I got these tendencies from you.

824
00:34:35,292 --> 00:34:36,392
- Really? - Yes.

825
00:34:36,392 --> 00:34:38,192
You're tenacious.

826
00:34:38,392 --> 00:34:41,062
- You received a trophy at work. - Yes.

827
00:34:41,462 --> 00:34:42,962
- Did you bring it? - I did. Yes.

828
00:34:43,632 --> 00:34:45,102
I received a trophy.

829
00:34:45,502 --> 00:34:48,032
- Do you want to see it? - I'll bring it.

830
00:34:49,772 --> 00:34:50,772
(My goodness)

831
00:34:53,312 --> 00:34:55,882
- Seriously, Dad. - Take a look.

832
00:34:57,612 --> 00:34:58,742
(Dad's trophy for 30 years of service)

833
00:34:58,742 --> 00:35:00,682
"The 30 years we've walked together..."

834
00:35:00,682 --> 00:35:01,852
"and the future we'll face."

835
00:35:01,852 --> 00:35:03,422
Director Choi Chang Ha.

836
00:35:03,422 --> 00:35:04,752
Your dad needs a round of applause.

837
00:35:04,752 --> 00:35:05,952
- Seriously. - At one company too.

838
00:35:05,952 --> 00:35:07,322
- Thank you. - Thank you.

839
00:35:07,822 --> 00:35:09,392
(Proud)

840
00:35:10,092 --> 00:35:11,462
- Keep eating. - Okay.

841
00:35:11,562 --> 00:35:12,792
I'll bring something.

842
00:35:12,792 --> 00:35:13,932
Put yourself at ease.

843
00:35:16,032 --> 00:35:18,232
(Hurrying over)

844
00:35:19,402 --> 00:35:20,402
(Rummaging)

845
00:35:20,402 --> 00:35:21,472
What?

846
00:35:23,202 --> 00:35:24,402
- Dad. - Yes?

847
00:35:25,602 --> 00:35:26,912
What? What's that?

848
00:35:26,912 --> 00:35:29,582
(What? What's that?)

849
00:35:29,882 --> 00:35:32,042
(Ta-da)

850
00:35:32,612 --> 00:35:33,782
Daughters are the best.

851
00:35:33,782 --> 00:35:34,912
- You're right. - What's that?

852
00:35:34,912 --> 00:35:36,482
I made it myself.

853
00:35:36,482 --> 00:35:37,752
(I made it for you, Dad.)

854
00:35:39,152 --> 00:35:41,622
- When you go to a pricey place, - Thank you.

855
00:35:41,622 --> 00:35:42,892
they give you a dessert with your name written on it.

856
00:35:42,892 --> 00:35:44,762
I wrote this writing at the bottom.

857
00:35:44,762 --> 00:35:46,262
(Cute)

858
00:35:46,262 --> 00:35:47,392
Make a wish.

859
00:35:47,392 --> 00:35:48,692
- A wish? - Yes.

860
00:35:48,932 --> 00:35:50,732
Close your eyes. Don't say it out loud.

861
00:35:50,732 --> 00:35:52,232
Let's make a wish together.

862
00:35:52,402 --> 00:35:53,502
Okay.

863
00:35:53,502 --> 00:35:55,772
(Closing his eyes)

864
00:35:56,542 --> 00:35:59,112
(She prepared a cake with respect for her dad.)

865
00:35:59,542 --> 00:36:01,872
(Clasping her hands together, she makes a wish with her dad.)

866
00:36:02,512 --> 00:36:04,812
- Thank you. - Thank you.

867
00:36:05,382 --> 00:36:06,952
Thank you. Should I blow out the candle?

868
00:36:06,952 --> 00:36:08,012
Yes.

869
00:36:09,322 --> 00:36:11,252
(Blowing)

870
00:36:11,752 --> 00:36:13,552
(Congratulations.)

871
00:36:13,552 --> 00:36:15,452
- You know... - You're handsome.

872
00:36:15,792 --> 00:36:17,322
(Embarrassed)

873
00:36:17,322 --> 00:36:18,492
No other daughter is as nice as her.

874
00:36:18,492 --> 00:36:19,632
Seriously. No other daughter is...

875
00:36:19,632 --> 00:36:20,732
- as nice as her. - Right.

876
00:36:21,162 --> 00:36:22,332
- She is the best. - Ta-da.

877
00:36:23,202 --> 00:36:25,532
- Try the strawberry cake. - Okay.

878
00:36:25,702 --> 00:36:27,372
Here.

879
00:36:27,372 --> 00:36:29,072
(She cuts a big piece.)

880
00:36:29,072 --> 00:36:30,802
Here. Give me a bite.

881
00:36:30,802 --> 00:36:32,242
(After the dad takes a bite, the daughter takes a bite.)

882
00:36:32,242 --> 00:36:33,312
My goodness.

883
00:36:34,612 --> 00:36:35,942
- You could... - What do you think?

884
00:36:36,882 --> 00:36:38,042
You could sell it.

885
00:36:38,042 --> 00:36:39,512
I made it well, right?

886
00:36:39,952 --> 00:36:41,082
- You could... - What do you think?

887
00:36:41,082 --> 00:36:42,952
It'll be so nice to have...

888
00:36:42,952 --> 00:36:44,852
a daughter with such incredible reactions.

889
00:36:45,082 --> 00:36:47,322
- My goodness. - Dad. Time out.

890
00:36:47,322 --> 00:36:48,722
Why was your reaction different when you had the chicken soup?

891
00:36:48,722 --> 00:36:49,762
What?

892
00:36:50,092 --> 00:36:52,562
- I could sell the cake, - It isn't like that.

893
00:36:52,562 --> 00:36:53,662
but the chicken soup...

894
00:36:53,662 --> 00:36:55,162
- He became flustered right away. - As for the chicken soup,

895
00:36:55,162 --> 00:36:56,802
- My dad can't lie. - it should be seasoned a bit more.

896
00:36:57,362 --> 00:36:59,172
- You said it was tasty. - It's tasty.

897
00:37:00,972 --> 00:37:02,602
(Although he said it was tasty, he ate slowly.)

898
00:37:02,902 --> 00:37:03,942
Seriously, Dad.

899
00:37:04,042 --> 00:37:07,472
(He even sprinkled pepper behind his daughter's back.)

900
00:37:07,812 --> 00:37:11,342
- I found the chicken soup tasty. - But... I found it tasty too.

901
00:37:11,912 --> 00:37:14,452
You have a talent for making cakes.

902
00:37:15,282 --> 00:37:16,582
"You have a talent for making cakes."

903
00:37:16,582 --> 00:37:18,852
- I mean... - Your reactions are so different.

904
00:37:18,852 --> 00:37:20,022
This is tasty.

905
00:37:20,152 --> 00:37:21,192
- It's tasty, right? - Yes.

906
00:37:21,752 --> 00:37:23,422
- It's tasty. - I found the chicken soup tasty.

907
00:37:23,992 --> 00:37:25,062
It's tasty.

908
00:37:27,762 --> 00:37:29,362
Where are you going after the meal?

909
00:37:29,362 --> 00:37:30,932
- Me? Yes. - Are you going home?

910
00:37:31,262 --> 00:37:32,332
Yes, I'm going home.

911
00:37:32,332 --> 00:37:34,902
- I need to go and work part-time. - Okay.

912
00:37:34,902 --> 00:37:36,942
- That day too? - Will you go and work part-time?

913
00:37:37,472 --> 00:37:39,542
Take care. Good luck.

914
00:37:39,542 --> 00:37:40,542
(Holding her hands tight)

915
00:37:40,642 --> 00:37:42,642
You're the star of the day, so don't do anything.

916
00:37:42,642 --> 00:37:44,582
- Thank you for the food. - Sit still...

917
00:37:44,712 --> 00:37:46,252
and look outside the window.

918
00:37:46,252 --> 00:37:48,012
- Enjoy the view. - I'll bring the plates to the sink.

919
00:37:48,012 --> 00:37:49,222
- No, you can't. - Really?

920
00:37:49,222 --> 00:37:51,322
- It's just that... - No.

921
00:37:51,552 --> 00:37:53,322
- Seriously. - Dad, enjoy the view.

922
00:37:53,774 --> 00:37:54,914
I'll look at Gamja.

923
00:37:55,844 --> 00:37:58,344
- Guests at my place can't move. - Gamja.

924
00:37:58,614 --> 00:37:59,914
- That's right. - I do everything.

925
00:38:00,084 --> 00:38:02,084
- It's easier that way. - The guests are the kings.

926
00:38:02,324 --> 00:38:05,254
You do things well by yourself.

927
00:38:05,254 --> 00:38:07,154
- You do the dishes well. - Of course.

928
00:38:07,154 --> 00:38:09,794
I can tell from her dad's eyes that he dotes on his daughter.

929
00:38:10,224 --> 00:38:11,824
I'm ready to get married.

930
00:38:12,264 --> 00:38:13,334
What?

931
00:38:14,834 --> 00:38:15,934
He doesn't like it.

932
00:38:15,934 --> 00:38:17,634
Tell him when you're seeing someone.

933
00:38:17,834 --> 00:38:20,034
My dad tells me not to get married.

934
00:38:20,034 --> 00:38:22,444
- Really? - He thinks I'm too good for anyone.

935
00:38:22,944 --> 00:38:24,074
- For real? - Dads are like that.

936
00:38:24,074 --> 00:38:25,344
- Why did you ask, "For real?" - What?

937
00:38:25,874 --> 00:38:27,974
- I can't let this go. - Seriously.

938
00:38:28,444 --> 00:38:29,684
(It's a misunderstanding.)

939
00:38:29,684 --> 00:38:31,384
- Why did you ask, "For real?" - I'm sorry.

940
00:38:31,544 --> 00:38:32,654
- This is... - Seriously.

941
00:38:32,954 --> 00:38:34,154
- I'm sorry. - I'm sorry, Shin Young.

942
00:38:34,154 --> 00:38:35,284
It's okay.

943
00:38:36,324 --> 00:38:37,454
I'm done with the dishes.

944
00:38:37,454 --> 00:38:38,584
- Are you done? - Yes.

945
00:38:38,994 --> 00:38:42,464
You've become neater since moving out,

946
00:38:42,564 --> 00:38:43,864
- right? - Of course.

947
00:38:45,564 --> 00:38:47,264
If I don't do it, no one else does.

948
00:38:47,634 --> 00:38:48,734
That's right.

949
00:38:49,634 --> 00:38:52,534
Dad, I need to get ready for my part-time job,

950
00:38:52,534 --> 00:38:55,334
- so you can leave first. - Okay.

951
00:38:56,144 --> 00:38:57,204
All right.

952
00:38:57,544 --> 00:38:59,374
Gosh, do you guys actually hug?

953
00:38:59,374 --> 00:39:00,674
- Of course. - It was nice.

954
00:39:00,944 --> 00:39:02,914
Dad, travel safely.

955
00:39:05,244 --> 00:39:06,684
- Dad. - I'm glad I bought water.

956
00:39:06,814 --> 00:39:07,914
- Bye. - I'll get going now.

957
00:39:08,784 --> 00:39:09,884
Bye.

958
00:39:10,624 --> 00:39:11,724
- My goodness. - What?

959
00:39:13,154 --> 00:39:14,424
- I mean... - A kiss on the cheek.

960
00:39:14,424 --> 00:39:15,664
A kiss on the cheek is rare.

961
00:39:15,664 --> 00:39:17,094
- I haven't seen it in a while. - In your 20s...

962
00:39:17,224 --> 00:39:18,894
- I haven't seen it in a while. - My goodness.

963
00:39:18,894 --> 00:39:20,664
We hug our parents...

964
00:39:20,664 --> 00:39:22,404
- or put our shoulders around them. - That's right. We do that much.

965
00:39:22,404 --> 00:39:23,764
- Really? - But a kiss on the cheek is...

966
00:39:24,104 --> 00:39:25,674
- Sons don't do that. - It's understandable.

967
00:39:25,674 --> 00:39:27,234
- How about, "Dad, I love you?" - I say that often.

968
00:39:27,234 --> 00:39:29,404
- Really? - I say that all the time.

969
00:39:29,844 --> 00:39:30,874
I stopped saying "Dad, I love you..."

970
00:39:30,874 --> 00:39:31,874
- in third grade. - Really?

971
00:39:32,344 --> 00:39:33,544
(Very mature)

972
00:39:33,544 --> 00:39:35,244
I wrote it in my letter from the army training center.

973
00:39:35,244 --> 00:39:36,384
- The army training center? - I cried.

974
00:39:36,944 --> 00:39:38,344
- When you came out... - You're less than human...

975
00:39:38,344 --> 00:39:39,814
if you don't write that there.

976
00:39:39,954 --> 00:39:41,554
- That's right. - Really?

977
00:39:41,784 --> 00:39:44,484
It could be a test to see if you're human or not.

978
00:39:45,084 --> 00:39:46,994
After getting drunk, I messaged my mom,

979
00:39:46,994 --> 00:39:48,794
- "Mom, I love you." - Gosh!

980
00:39:48,794 --> 00:39:49,864
She left me on read.

981
00:39:51,424 --> 00:39:53,094
- She felt awkward. - That's right.

982
00:39:53,094 --> 00:39:54,164
She left me on read.

983
00:39:54,394 --> 00:39:56,164
(Did she think it was a spam message?)

984
00:39:56,164 --> 00:39:57,264
- Bye. - I'll get going now.

985
00:39:57,904 --> 00:39:59,174
- Bye. - Thank you.

986
00:39:59,934 --> 00:40:01,074
- It's such a heartwarming sight. - Thank you.

987
00:40:01,074 --> 00:40:02,474
Such interactions are rare.

988
00:40:02,474 --> 00:40:03,544
- Really? - Come again.

989
00:40:03,544 --> 00:40:05,344
Dad does that to Mom.

990
00:40:05,344 --> 00:40:06,844
- It makes sense. - That's right.

991
00:40:06,844 --> 00:40:07,944
That's right.

992
00:40:08,544 --> 00:40:09,884
Dad, take care.

993
00:40:13,454 --> 00:40:16,084
(The sun sets.)

994
00:40:18,084 --> 00:40:20,224
- I'm on my way to work part-time. - You're on your way.

995
00:40:23,224 --> 00:40:25,834
(Taking big steps)

996
00:40:26,794 --> 00:40:29,734
Today, I got to immerse myself...

997
00:40:29,734 --> 00:40:31,804
in my life.

998
00:40:32,234 --> 00:40:34,574
"I'm living diligently all day."

999
00:40:34,574 --> 00:40:36,474
I felt that today.

1000
00:40:37,004 --> 00:40:40,174
There has been a major change after moving out.

1001
00:40:40,774 --> 00:40:43,944
- Mom and Dad aren't with me. - That's right.

1002
00:40:44,144 --> 00:40:46,284
- They aren't with you. - No one carries heavy items for me.

1003
00:40:46,654 --> 00:40:50,124
If I put my socks somewhere...

1004
00:40:50,554 --> 00:40:52,894
and look at the spot again after taking a short rest,

1005
00:40:52,894 --> 00:40:54,254
they're still there.

1006
00:40:54,624 --> 00:40:56,124
No one picks them up for me.

1007
00:40:56,364 --> 00:40:57,924
I learned that by heart.

1008
00:40:58,124 --> 00:41:01,364
That's why I'm learning to do things myself.

1009
00:41:01,364 --> 00:41:02,534
You need to do things yourself.

1010
00:41:03,504 --> 00:41:06,174
(She is building her own daily life.)

1011
00:41:08,674 --> 00:41:09,904
(She continues to fill her days.)

1012
00:41:09,904 --> 00:41:12,144
I want to work hard.

1013
00:41:14,974 --> 00:41:16,044
Do you keep studying?

1014
00:41:16,044 --> 00:41:17,714
- Yes, there are many lines. - On your way?

1015
00:41:17,714 --> 00:41:18,784
The lines.

1016
00:41:20,914 --> 00:41:23,124
(Ji Su's Happiness Is Sailing Smoothly)

1017
00:41:23,124 --> 00:41:24,184
I want to keep watching.

1018
00:41:24,184 --> 00:41:26,624
- How about the part-time job? - I wanted to watch her work.

1019
00:41:26,924 --> 00:41:29,224
- We enjoyed the video. - Seriously.

1020
00:41:29,224 --> 00:41:30,294
Thank you.

1021
00:41:31,124 --> 00:41:32,664
How did it feel to watch your daily life?

1022
00:41:33,034 --> 00:41:34,934
It was fascinating to see myself on TV.

1023
00:41:34,934 --> 00:41:37,264
Your continuous reactions...

1024
00:41:37,264 --> 00:41:39,904
- felt so genuine. - Yes, they were totally genuine.

1025
00:41:39,904 --> 00:41:41,474
That made me tear up even more.

1026
00:41:41,474 --> 00:41:43,074
- They were totally genuine. - Right.

1027
00:41:43,344 --> 00:41:46,244
- It was a truly independent life. - Seriously.

1028
00:41:46,244 --> 00:41:48,774
What Shin Young said on the show...

1029
00:41:48,774 --> 00:41:50,044
went viral on the internet.

1030
00:41:50,384 --> 00:41:53,084
- "Only you can help yourself." - No one else can do it.

1031
00:41:53,084 --> 00:41:54,484
Ji Su lives that life.

1032
00:41:54,684 --> 00:41:56,054
- I love it. - She is the perfect example.

1033
00:41:56,054 --> 00:41:58,484
I learn many things by watching Shin Young on TV.

1034
00:41:58,784 --> 00:42:00,394
She is like the adult version of myself.

1035
00:42:01,854 --> 00:42:04,024
Gosh, I'll need to stay alert and live well.

1036
00:42:05,594 --> 00:42:06,794
I'll need to do that.

1037
00:42:06,794 --> 00:42:08,134
(The adult becomes solemn.)

1038
00:42:08,294 --> 00:42:09,564
Personally, I thought...

1039
00:42:09,964 --> 00:42:13,234
- it was the essence of life. - I know.

1040
00:42:13,234 --> 00:42:15,474
Her daily life had the joys and sorrows.

1041
00:42:15,704 --> 00:42:17,374
"I Live Alone" needed...

1042
00:42:17,374 --> 00:42:19,174
- I know. - a guest like her.

1043
00:42:19,844 --> 00:42:22,244
When I star in an audition show once in a while,

1044
00:42:22,614 --> 00:42:25,214
I see people who have lived...

1045
00:42:25,214 --> 00:42:28,384
every day to the fullest.

1046
00:42:28,384 --> 00:42:29,824
- That's right. - If you live that way,

1047
00:42:30,184 --> 00:42:32,084
you'll have many materials...

1048
00:42:32,324 --> 00:42:34,524
you can use no matter what you do...

1049
00:42:34,524 --> 00:42:35,924
- in the future. - I know.

1050
00:42:36,224 --> 00:42:39,994
I think now is her time to use those materials.

1051
00:42:39,994 --> 00:42:41,734
- So... - She has strength.

1052
00:42:41,734 --> 00:42:44,304
Given her personality...

1053
00:42:46,704 --> 00:42:48,274
- You said such nice things. - It's my part-time job...

1054
00:42:48,274 --> 00:42:49,444
to pass the tissue paper today.

1055
00:42:49,444 --> 00:42:51,374
- You said such nice things. - My goodness.

1056
00:42:51,574 --> 00:42:52,914
I just want to let you know...

1057
00:42:53,814 --> 00:42:56,144
that you need to challenge yourself recklessly now.

1058
00:42:56,144 --> 00:42:57,544
I have the same advice.

1059
00:42:57,544 --> 00:42:59,984
You should find your tastes...

1060
00:43:00,214 --> 00:43:02,114
and focus on yourself.

1061
00:43:02,314 --> 00:43:03,554
"What do I like?"

1062
00:43:03,554 --> 00:43:04,984
"What do I want to do if I have money?"

1063
00:43:04,984 --> 00:43:07,094
I hope you'll think about that.

1064
00:43:07,094 --> 00:43:09,524
- You're living too diligently. - I agree.

1065
00:43:09,664 --> 00:43:11,624
You failed to win the Best Rookie Award,

1066
00:43:11,624 --> 00:43:13,564
but better awards will come your way.

1067
00:43:13,564 --> 00:43:14,834
Your words make me feel like...

1068
00:43:14,834 --> 00:43:17,564
- I've won an award. - But you need an actual award.

1069
00:43:19,234 --> 00:43:21,274
Forget about feeling like you've won an award.

1070
00:43:21,274 --> 00:43:22,444
I hate that the most.

1071
00:43:23,204 --> 00:43:25,374
When you're a nominee, they film you nonstop.

1072
00:43:25,374 --> 00:43:27,114
"You're the winner in my heart" is even more aggravating.

1073
00:43:27,114 --> 00:43:28,144
I hate that the most.

1074
00:43:28,144 --> 00:43:30,584
"You're the first-place winner in my heart."

1075
00:43:30,584 --> 00:43:31,584
That's the worst.

1076
00:43:31,584 --> 00:43:34,354
- I just want to win first place. - People don't think I deserve it.

1077
00:43:34,354 --> 00:43:35,554
- That's right. - Yes.

1078
00:43:35,854 --> 00:43:37,384
- That's exactly it. - Yes.

1079
00:43:37,584 --> 00:43:40,394
Win an award. Seriously.

1080
00:43:40,724 --> 00:43:43,594
- You'll have a nice life. - A very nice life.

1081
00:43:43,664 --> 00:43:44,894
We will root for you!

1082
00:43:44,894 --> 00:43:46,034
- Good luck! - Good luck!

1083
00:43:46,034 --> 00:43:47,034
(I Live Alone)

1084
00:43:47,334 --> 00:43:50,564
(Thorough Cleaning)

1085
00:43:52,164 --> 00:43:54,504
(Sung Hwan is fast asleep.)

1086
00:43:57,104 --> 00:44:00,974
(Tossing and turning)

1087
00:44:03,944 --> 00:44:05,884
Gosh, the time is...

1088
00:44:11,154 --> 00:44:14,154
(He barely manages to get himself up.)

1089
00:44:17,094 --> 00:44:19,734
- He slept outside! - So he sleeps outside.

1090
00:44:21,164 --> 00:44:23,404
(Unlike with the fairly dull color from the past,)

1091
00:44:25,874 --> 00:44:27,474
(the rooftop looks a lot brighter in pink.)

1092
00:44:27,474 --> 00:44:29,274
The rooftop is in pink now!

1093
00:44:29,274 --> 00:44:31,304
Right. I love pink.

1094
00:44:31,304 --> 00:44:35,884
(He has everything that is needed to sleep outside.)

1095
00:44:37,914 --> 00:44:38,984
(He also has items...)

1096
00:44:38,984 --> 00:44:40,054
Gosh, check out the vibes.

1097
00:44:40,054 --> 00:44:41,984
- Gosh, they're items from the past. - That's great.

1098
00:44:41,984 --> 00:44:42,984
(that bring up the vibes.)

1099
00:44:43,854 --> 00:44:45,854
(Sung Hwan's brand new hideout)

1100
00:44:46,094 --> 00:44:48,994
From around April to the middle of June,

1101
00:44:48,994 --> 00:44:50,894
I sleep outside from time to time depending on the weather.

1102
00:44:50,894 --> 00:44:52,864
- That sounds great. - I'm so jealous.

1103
00:44:52,864 --> 00:44:54,194
It will feel cozy. I'm so jealous.

1104
00:44:54,464 --> 00:44:58,064
I hear songs on the radio.

1105
00:44:58,064 --> 00:45:01,274
I'm not sure which direction it comes from,

1106
00:45:01,274 --> 00:45:03,374
- but I can feel the breeze. - That must feel nice.

1107
00:45:03,374 --> 00:45:04,974
I personally also like the smell...

1108
00:45:04,974 --> 00:45:06,074
- of the mosquito coil. - The mosquito coil!

1109
00:45:06,074 --> 00:45:09,884
I love it when these three things are felt.

1110
00:45:10,184 --> 00:45:11,684
I think that is why I sleep outside from time to time.

1111
00:45:11,684 --> 00:45:12,784
(He sleeps on the rooftop from time to time!)

1112
00:45:14,054 --> 00:45:17,584
(Which channel should I listen to today?)

1113
00:45:17,584 --> 00:45:20,154
We saw this scenery back when we were in elementary school.

1114
00:45:20,154 --> 00:45:21,194
There were men who looked just like that.

1115
00:45:21,194 --> 00:45:22,564
It feels exactly like "Under the Same Roof."

1116
00:45:22,564 --> 00:45:23,764
Right!

1117
00:45:23,764 --> 00:45:24,794
It feels like the house from back then.

1118
00:45:24,794 --> 00:45:25,864
Right.

1119
00:45:28,464 --> 00:45:31,334
(On one side of the cozy rooftop,)

1120
00:45:32,634 --> 00:45:34,774
Gosh, the ice still hasn't melted.

1121
00:45:34,774 --> 00:45:35,804
(Father Ku takes something out.)

1122
00:45:37,144 --> 00:45:39,314
- The ice still hasn't melted. - Cassia seed tea!

1123
00:45:39,874 --> 00:45:41,214
- With that, - Sometimes, I...

1124
00:45:41,214 --> 00:45:43,284
you can mix in rice and make it cold.

1125
00:45:43,414 --> 00:45:46,684
You can eat it with cucumber kimchi or aged kimchi.

1126
00:45:46,854 --> 00:45:50,224
You can eat it with cucumber kimchi or aged kimchi.

1127
00:45:50,284 --> 00:45:52,024
They should be cut vertically.

1128
00:45:52,024 --> 00:45:53,654
- Get used to it, Dowoon. - Gosh.

1129
00:45:53,654 --> 00:45:55,354
- It tastes great like that. - Right.

1130
00:45:55,354 --> 00:45:57,724
- Focus on her words. - That sounds amazing.

1131
00:45:57,724 --> 00:45:58,964
- She says a lot of great things. - Can I put on...

1132
00:45:58,964 --> 00:46:00,194
my AirPod on the left?

1133
00:46:00,594 --> 00:46:01,634
- Just the left. - You can't do that.

1134
00:46:01,634 --> 00:46:02,634
You can never do that. You have to...

1135
00:46:02,634 --> 00:46:03,764
- listen to her. - That will make me feel upset.

1136
00:46:03,764 --> 00:46:04,964
I'll still be able to listen.

1137
00:46:04,964 --> 00:46:07,434
- I just listened to her, - It will taste amazing like that.

1138
00:46:07,834 --> 00:46:09,344
but I can picture things around my mouth.

1139
00:46:09,344 --> 00:46:11,304
- Just like that. - The kimchi is torn like this.

1140
00:46:11,304 --> 00:46:12,974
- After wrapping it around... - Were the two of you close?

1141
00:46:12,974 --> 00:46:14,174
- They're like siblings. - No.

1142
00:46:14,174 --> 00:46:16,044
We met each other for the first time through I Live Alone.

1143
00:46:16,744 --> 00:46:18,044
We get along with each other so well.

1144
00:46:18,044 --> 00:46:19,484
They feel like high school friends.

1145
00:46:19,484 --> 00:46:20,814
- We're the Pepper Siblings. - Right.

1146
00:46:20,814 --> 00:46:22,154
Right. We both love pepper.

1147
00:46:24,154 --> 00:46:25,924
(Picking up)

1148
00:46:28,024 --> 00:46:30,894
(Pouring)

1149
00:46:33,894 --> 00:46:34,994
(He starts with a cold glass of cassia seed tea.)

1150
00:46:34,994 --> 00:46:36,404
The vibes, Sung Hwan!

1151
00:46:36,664 --> 00:46:37,804
I love the vibes.

1152
00:46:40,134 --> 00:46:42,474
(On the open rooftop,)

1153
00:46:42,704 --> 00:46:45,704
(he enjoys the morning of early summer.)

1154
00:46:47,274 --> 00:46:50,944
(Humming)

1155
00:46:50,944 --> 00:46:52,314
Gosh, Dad!

1156
00:46:53,054 --> 00:46:55,114
- Soon Dol's father! - Dad! Father!

1157
00:46:55,114 --> 00:46:57,354
- Where's Soon Dol? - Mom wants you to come down!

1158
00:46:57,654 --> 00:46:59,454
(Is that so?)

1159
00:47:00,594 --> 00:47:02,764
(While ignoring his wife's call,)

1160
00:47:02,894 --> 00:47:04,994
(he grabs the instant coffee.)

1161
00:47:06,394 --> 00:47:07,594
(Pouring the cold instant coffee)

1162
00:47:07,594 --> 00:47:09,464
Instant coffee with ice!

1163
00:47:09,464 --> 00:47:11,264
Right. The ice melted as I made it the day before.

1164
00:47:11,264 --> 00:47:12,334
That's amazing.

1165
00:47:12,334 --> 00:47:15,904
(A sweet charge of morning caffeine)

1166
00:47:15,904 --> 00:47:18,504
Dipping some sponge cake into that is the best!

1167
00:47:19,104 --> 00:47:21,474
- I'm serious. - I just want it separately.

1168
00:47:21,474 --> 00:47:22,684
You should give that a try.

1169
00:47:22,684 --> 00:47:24,244
How are we supposed to remember all of that?

1170
00:47:24,244 --> 00:47:26,214
- Get used to it, Dowoon. - Right.

1171
00:47:26,384 --> 00:47:28,184
I love it.

1172
00:47:28,354 --> 00:47:30,924
- You say you love everything! - I love the vibes.

1173
00:47:30,924 --> 00:47:32,584
Grow out your hair just on the right side.

1174
00:47:32,584 --> 00:47:33,994
(Joking)

1175
00:47:34,554 --> 00:47:35,854
Then I'll move to his left.

1176
00:47:38,524 --> 00:47:41,394
(His happy tea time comes to an end.)

1177
00:47:41,634 --> 00:47:42,834
(He gets his things and hurries down.)

1178
00:47:42,834 --> 00:47:44,534
I have a lot to do.

1179
00:47:44,534 --> 00:47:46,104
(I'm busy.)

1180
00:47:46,834 --> 00:47:47,874
First of all...

1181
00:47:52,714 --> 00:47:54,914
(He turns on the lights of his bedroom first.)

1182
00:47:57,344 --> 00:47:59,284
Wait. What's that?

1183
00:47:59,284 --> 00:48:00,284
(What are those things placed on one side of the wall?)

1184
00:48:00,284 --> 00:48:02,554
It's the Ku Zone. A place of my own.

1185
00:48:03,524 --> 00:48:05,624
After walking 446km,

1186
00:48:06,054 --> 00:48:08,724
I placed the outfit I wore on the wall.

1187
00:48:08,724 --> 00:48:10,594
- I see. - Mr. Ku Zone.

1188
00:48:10,794 --> 00:48:12,224
We can do it!

1189
00:48:12,224 --> 00:48:15,134
(The moments of the cross-country march)

1190
00:48:15,664 --> 00:48:17,104
My shoes are placed at the bottom.

1191
00:48:17,404 --> 00:48:19,164
I signed them myself. I wrote down "446km," the distance I went,

1192
00:48:19,164 --> 00:48:20,934
and my name, "Ku Sung Hwan."

1193
00:48:21,674 --> 00:48:23,444
When I open my eyes in the morning,

1194
00:48:23,644 --> 00:48:26,874
it makes me think, "I can do anything today."

1195
00:48:27,044 --> 00:48:28,574
That's the thought I get every morning...

1196
00:48:28,574 --> 00:48:30,884
- after setting up that spot. - The Ku Zone.

1197
00:48:31,144 --> 00:48:32,314
That's so impressive.

1198
00:48:32,314 --> 00:48:33,454
(Full of respect)

1199
00:48:35,414 --> 00:48:36,624
(Grabbing)

1200
00:48:38,624 --> 00:48:41,324
(He throws down the blanket after curling it up.)

1201
00:48:41,324 --> 00:48:43,164
(Grabbing)

1202
00:48:44,824 --> 00:48:46,234
(Is he also taking out the mattress cover?)

1203
00:48:46,234 --> 00:48:47,634
- The mattress cover? - Gosh!

1204
00:48:49,904 --> 00:48:52,834
Thank you for serving me for all this time, mattress.

1205
00:48:52,904 --> 00:48:54,704
- Are you changing your mattress? - That must be it.

1206
00:48:55,474 --> 00:48:56,874
With how much I weigh,

1207
00:48:57,174 --> 00:49:00,644
the springs pop out after around three years.

1208
00:49:00,844 --> 00:49:03,844
- It's of no use after four years. - Right.

1209
00:49:03,844 --> 00:49:05,784
But as that mattress stayed with me for five years,

1210
00:49:06,114 --> 00:49:08,784
it was like a soldier that fought 1,000 battles.

1211
00:49:08,784 --> 00:49:10,684
- That was how much it went through. - Really?

1212
00:49:10,684 --> 00:49:12,584
There will be parts that sink in after that long.

1213
00:49:12,584 --> 00:49:16,094
(After many fierce battles...)

1214
00:49:17,224 --> 00:49:19,094
It has scars everywhere.

1215
00:49:19,664 --> 00:49:21,894
It's full of scars.

1216
00:49:21,894 --> 00:49:23,404
So mattresses are consumables.

1217
00:49:23,404 --> 00:49:24,564
- Of course. - They have to be changed.

1218
00:49:24,564 --> 00:49:25,564
They have to be changed.

1219
00:49:25,804 --> 00:49:28,234
My friend who lived with me...

1220
00:49:28,234 --> 00:49:30,374
peed on it many times...

1221
00:49:30,374 --> 00:49:31,744
- when she was young. - Right.

1222
00:49:31,744 --> 00:49:32,744
- Puppies do that. - And...

1223
00:49:33,014 --> 00:49:35,244
there are vomit stains as well.

1224
00:49:35,874 --> 00:49:37,844
After much consideration,

1225
00:49:37,844 --> 00:49:39,884
I decided to...

1226
00:49:40,954 --> 00:49:43,724
go for a replash.

1227
00:49:44,024 --> 00:49:45,624
- That's why I'm going to change it. - What's "replash?"

1228
00:49:48,524 --> 00:49:49,864
You should replash your mind.

1229
00:49:49,864 --> 00:49:52,834
The reason for that... Let's move on.

1230
00:49:55,564 --> 00:49:58,704
(The replash is going smoothly.)

1231
00:49:58,734 --> 00:50:00,034
My gosh.

1232
00:50:01,374 --> 00:50:03,044
Gosh, Kkotbun.

1233
00:50:05,444 --> 00:50:07,114
(Tapping)

1234
00:50:09,744 --> 00:50:12,714
(I've used it for a long time.)

1235
00:50:14,614 --> 00:50:18,154
(Heave-ho!)

1236
00:50:20,324 --> 00:50:22,094
(Grabbing)

1237
00:50:24,194 --> 00:50:26,594
(He cleans the bottom of the bed while he's at it.)

1238
00:50:26,594 --> 00:50:28,464
The bottom of the bed looks really clean.

1239
00:50:28,464 --> 00:50:29,664
I cleaned the bottom...

1240
00:50:29,664 --> 00:50:30,904
- You did? - from time to time.

1241
00:50:31,034 --> 00:50:33,404
When you start coughing for some reason in a clean house,

1242
00:50:33,404 --> 00:50:35,234
- you have to check down there. - Right.

1243
00:50:38,374 --> 00:50:39,514
Gosh, there we go.

1244
00:50:40,414 --> 00:50:42,714
Sung Hwan is so neat.

1245
00:50:42,714 --> 00:50:44,184
(He heads to the living room after cleaning the room.)

1246
00:50:47,254 --> 00:50:50,584
(He makes a call to someone.)

1247
00:50:51,654 --> 00:50:54,124
- I have arrived. - I'll go down, sir.

1248
00:50:54,354 --> 00:50:55,524
- Okay. - Right.

1249
00:50:57,064 --> 00:50:59,464
(Let's hurry down.)

1250
00:51:02,094 --> 00:51:04,534
(Hurrying down)

1251
00:51:06,164 --> 00:51:07,804
(Opening)

1252
00:51:10,174 --> 00:51:11,604
(Looking around)

1253
00:51:11,604 --> 00:51:12,604
Oh, hello.

1254
00:51:13,344 --> 00:51:14,974
- You're from the mattress company. - Right.

1255
00:51:15,144 --> 00:51:16,884
- The mattress is here. - It's a pleasure to meet you.

1256
00:51:17,014 --> 00:51:18,984
You feel this excitement when you bring in new furniture.

1257
00:51:18,984 --> 00:51:20,754
- Right. I felt so excited. - Right.

1258
00:51:20,754 --> 00:51:22,754
- It feels like a new start. - A new start.

1259
00:51:22,754 --> 00:51:23,784
Right.

1260
00:51:25,854 --> 00:51:27,624
(They bring it down slowly.)

1261
00:51:27,624 --> 00:51:29,254
- We'll try to bring it down first. - Gosh.

1262
00:51:29,254 --> 00:51:31,164
- It was really heavy. - It must be really heavy.

1263
00:51:31,164 --> 00:51:32,264
You bought a big one.

1264
00:51:33,264 --> 00:51:36,634
The width of the mattress was 1.5m.

1265
00:51:36,904 --> 00:51:40,474
The width of the windows of my house is 1m.

1266
00:51:40,674 --> 00:51:45,044
It was impossible to bring in through the windows.

1267
00:51:45,474 --> 00:51:48,074
- I think it will be possible. - It's impossible.

1268
00:51:48,074 --> 00:51:49,914
I've tried everything to make it work.

1269
00:51:50,284 --> 00:51:54,014
I explained everything in advance...

1270
00:51:54,054 --> 00:51:56,454
that we had to carry it up...

1271
00:51:56,724 --> 00:51:57,954
There's no elevator at my place.

1272
00:51:57,954 --> 00:51:58,984
- from the... - It must be really tough...

1273
00:51:58,984 --> 00:52:00,024
- first floor. - to go up with that.

1274
00:52:01,124 --> 00:52:05,724
As I feel bad about this, I'll move to the tougher side.

1275
00:52:09,364 --> 00:52:10,364
(He even brought down the man of 100kg.)

1276
00:52:10,364 --> 00:52:11,634
- The Rainbow Cheonha Champion. - Gosh!

1277
00:52:11,704 --> 00:52:14,034
- That's impressive. - I'm sorry, Jang Woo.

1278
00:52:14,034 --> 00:52:16,944
(Rainbow Cheonha Champion, Ku Sung Hwan)

1279
00:52:18,244 --> 00:52:20,444
(I'll use more of my strength.)

1280
00:52:20,444 --> 00:52:22,874
Then you should lift it up from the bottom for us.

1281
00:52:22,874 --> 00:52:23,884
- Should I do that? - Yes.

1282
00:52:24,244 --> 00:52:25,244
One, two, three.

1283
00:52:25,784 --> 00:52:27,154
- That must be tough. - Gosh!

1284
00:52:27,454 --> 00:52:29,414
It must be hard as there's no place to hold onto.

1285
00:52:30,324 --> 00:52:31,854
This is really heavy!

1286
00:52:33,194 --> 00:52:34,254
I'm sorry.

1287
00:52:35,994 --> 00:52:37,864
We'll bring it down here.

1288
00:52:37,864 --> 00:52:38,894
(He feels flustered as it's heavier than he thought.)

1289
00:52:38,894 --> 00:52:40,034
(Bringing his head down)

1290
00:52:40,794 --> 00:52:42,634
- The fifth floor? - Yes.

1291
00:52:43,434 --> 00:52:44,864
- The fifth floor. - Gosh.

1292
00:52:45,004 --> 00:52:46,504
- I'm sorry. - It's tough without an elevator.

